{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the exiles of</b> — Rabbi Moses said: the exile that they began to deport. And Rabbi Marinus said: כי החל is like ויאבל חיל וחומה (Lamentations 2:8), and the meaning is: when the city is captured and those within it are killed, even the fugitives did not escape — only a few who were with the army." "<b>who are Canaanites</b> — We heard from the mouths of great ones that the land of Almania is the Canaanites who fled before the children of Israel when they came into the land, and likewise France is Pharnasia. And the Targum of Jonathan ben Uzziel: Sepharad is Aspamia, and this is the exile of Titus, and this prophecy is for the future. Not as Rabbi Moses said, for then they were scattered from the First Temple."], :book :obadiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Rabbi Moses refers to Ibn Ezra's older contemporary Moses ha-Kohen; Rabbi Marinus is likely Marinus of Neaples, a known correspondent.", 1 "Almania = Germany; Pharnasia = France; Aspamia = Spain, following Targum Jonathan on Sepharad."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Obadiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=18&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:37.728501548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}